cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HELIOS-L1 in your work, please cite it, together with the data sets and the papers of the models it lists for each result."
title: "HELIOS-L1: Heliophysical Exploration, Lagrange-1 Interplanetary Observation & Space-weather Suite"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aggarwal
    given-names: Keshav
    email: keshavaggarwal2310@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
abstract: >-
  HELIOS-L1 is a desktop application for space weather. It reads live solar wind
  measurements from the spacecraft at the Sun-Earth L1 point (NOAA RTSW) and archived
  data from NASA CDAWeb, OMNI, GFZ and NOAA SWPC, and runs published models on them:
  NOAA storm scales, magnetopause and bow shock positions, ring current (Dst) models,
  the auroral oval, CME arrival (drag-based model), shock normals, minimum variance,
  de Hoffmann-Teller and flux rope fits, superposed epoch analysis, OMNI statistics
  since 1963, PFSS coronal fields and radio occultation geometry with SPICE. Every
  result lists its data sources and can be exported. Builds for Windows, macOS and Linux.
repository-code: "https://github.com/jovian-explorer/HELIOS-L1"
keywords:
  - space weather
  - heliophysics
  - solar wind
  - geomagnetic storms
  - Sun-Earth L1
  - coronal mass ejections
